{#- List date cell reading ABSOLUTE first, relative second.

    The shared zenitcms:cell/datetime renders a lone pl-relative-time, so a date column
    says "in 2 months" and hides the day itself in a hover title. A certificate list is
    read to plan a renewal window, which needs the calendar day; "in 2 months" alone
    answers a different question and a tooltip is not a reading. The state record is the
    SAME DateTimeCellState the shared cell takes, so nothing about the data shape forks.

    The absolute half resolves in the VIEWER's zone through Dates.wallText, which reads
    the zn-tz preference off the render context -- never a server-side format. -#}
{% declare value: DateTimeCellState = null %}
{% if value != null %}
<span class="hh-cell-datetime" data-datetime={% value.iso %}>{{ Dates.wallText(value.iso) }}
    <span class="hh-muted">(<pl-relative-time datetime={% value.iso %} wording={% value.wording %}></pl-relative-time>)</span></span>
{% /if %}
